title: January 2026

@p2050_leadership_2026
# prose-audit: Grade A — Hołownia's departure and both successors are introduced through their party roles, the result is narrated without exposing the scoring model, and every Lewica response has an authored factional consequence.
title: Poland 2050 chooses a successor
subtitle: Pełczyńska-Nałęcz and Hennig-Kloska inherit Hołownia's party—but not his personal authority
face-image: img/poland/events/pres-candidate-holownia.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 28
order: 10
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2026 and month = 1 and (p2050_succession_opened = 1 or p2050_leader != "Szymon Hołownia" or p2050_holownia_retention_roll >= p2050_holownia_retention_ceiling)
on-arrival: {!
Q.p2050_succession_opened = 2;
const p2050LeadershipRoll =
    Math.floor((this.random.uint32() / 4294967296) * 17) - 8;
const pelczynskaScore =
    (Number(Q.p2050_state_capacity_share) || 0) +
    (Number(Q.p2050_relation) || 0) * 0.08 +
    p2050LeadershipRoll;
const hennigScore =
    (Number(Q.p2050_christian_dem_share) || 0) +
    (Number(Q.p2050_personalist_share) || 0) * 0.45 -
    p2050LeadershipRoll;
Q.p2050_leadership_pelczynska_score =
    Math.max(1, Math.round(pelczynskaScore));
Q.p2050_leadership_hennig_score =
    Math.max(1, Math.round(hennigScore));
Q.p2050_leader =
    pelczynskaScore >= hennigScore
        ? "Katarzyna Pełczyńska-Nałęcz"
        : "Paulina Hennig-Kloska";
Q.p2050_incoming_bloc =
    Q.p2050_leader == "Katarzyna Pełczyńska-Nałęcz"
        ? "state-capacity reformers, policy staff and members prioritising organisational autonomy"
        : "green centrists, cabinet pragmatists and MPs prioritising a broader electoral shelter";
Q.p2050_leadership_margin = Math.abs(
    Q.p2050_leadership_pelczynska_score -
    Q.p2050_leadership_hennig_score
);
Q.p2050_coalition_dissent += Math.max(
    3,
    13 - Math.min(10, Q.p2050_leadership_margin)
);
Q.news_headline =
    Q.p2050_leader + " wins the Poland 2050 leadership";
!}

= January 2026 — A successor and an unsettled electoral pact

The delegates applaud <span class="party-p2050"><b>Szymon Hołownia</b></span>, founder of Poland 2050, for longer
than either candidate. [? if president_name = "Szymon Hołownia": He leaves the
party chair because the President cannot conduct daily factional management
from the Palace.?]

[? if pres_2025_centre_candidate = "Szymon Hołownia" and president_name !=
"Szymon Hołownia": Hołownia's presidential defeat and the loss of the Sejm
marshal's chair have ended his claim to be both the party's face and its
permanent organiser.?]

[? if pres_2025_centre_candidate = "Ryszard Petru" and pres_2025_winner_key !=
"holownia": Petru's presidential defeat and the loss of the Sejm marshal's
chair leave Hołownia surrendering a party whose ballot he did not carry.?]

[? if pres_2025_centre_candidate = "Ryszard Petru" and pres_2025_winner_key =
"holownia": Petru governs from the Palace while Hołownia leaves the party
chair; Poland 2050 must separate presidential authority from its founder's
organisation.?]

[? if pres_2025_stanowski_breakout = 1: The contest also begins after
Stanowski turned Kanał Zero into a presidential electorate. Poland 2050's old
claim on voters outside both blocs now faces a measured competitor with more
media capacity and no coalition compromises to defend.?]

The succession offers two different kinds of survival. **Katarzyna
Pełczyńska-Nałęcz**, Poland 2050's state-capacity strategist, promises an
autonomous organisation with policy staff of its own. **Paulina
Hennig-Kloska**, the party's green and cabinet-facing organiser, argues for a
wider electoral shelter and fewer tests of ideological purity.

The membership gives **[+ p2050_leader +]** the chair. The incoming coalition
is made up of **[+ p2050_incoming_bloc +]**.[? if p2050_leadership_margin <= 4:
 The count is close enough that the defeated camp can obstruct every list and
staffing decision.?][? if p2050_leadership_margin > 4: The margin is clear, but
not large enough to turn the losing wing into spectators.?]

[? if ministry_p2050_in_cabinet: Poland 2050 shares cabinet responsibility, so
Lewica will meet the winner across the coalition table before
either party reaches a campaign rally.?][? if not ministry_p2050_in_cabinet:
Poland 2050 remains a parliamentary competitor and possible future partner;
Lewica has influence, not ownership, over what comes next.?] Our earlier line
on Third Way was **[+ third_way_response +]**. The new chair will read it as
either good faith, indifference or an invitation to raid the defeated wing.

- @p2050_accept
- @p2050_mediate
- @p2050_exploit

@p2050_accept
title: Recognise the winner and negotiate a delivery protocol
subtitle: Give the new chair room to govern, while making ministers and parliamentary negotiators report to the same agreement.
on-arrival: p2050_relation += 5; p2050_coalition_dissent -= 2; third_way_cohesion += 2 if third_way_active = 1; public_trust += 1; government_coalition_dissent += 1; news_headline = "The Left treats Poland 2050's result as valid and fragile"

Lewica congratulates **[+ p2050_leader +]** without pretending the losing camp
has disappeared. A short protocol names who may negotiate policy, lists and
cabinet disputes for Poland 2050. The winner gains breathing room; our own
coalition partners notice that another chair has received a separate channel.

- @poland_event_queue: File the delivery protocol

@p2050_mediate
title: Offer both camps a neutral coalition mediation
subtitle: Lend party staff to a reconciliation that may stabilise the centre and irritate KO.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The party cannot staff another partner's reconciliation.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; p2050_relation += 4; p2050_coalition_dissent -= 5; third_way_cohesion += 4 if third_way_active = 1; ko_relation -= 1; public_trust += 2; news_headline = "A coalition mediation postpones the centrist rupture"

Pełczyńska-Nałęcz and Hennig-Kloska send representatives to a Lewica-chaired
room and emerge with a division of party work neither can call surrender. The
truce does not erase the ballot, but it keeps local lists and parliamentary
votes from becoming immediate reprisals. KO dislikes seeing the Left become the
centre's indispensable broker.

- @poland_event_queue: Convene the mediation

@p2050_exploit
title: Recruit local and parliamentary defectors before the split
subtitle: Turn the losing camp's fear into organisers and councillors, accepting that both wings will call it a raid.
on-arrival: local_network += 3; p2050_relation -= 9; p2050_coalition_dissent += 7; third_way_cohesion -= 8 if third_way_active = 1; party_unity += 1; public_trust -= 2; news_headline = "The Left treats a coalition partner's weakness as an organisational opening"

Lewica's regional secretaries telephone the defeated camp before its new chair
can offer guarantees. Several organisers and councillors agree to talks; no
parliamentary mandate moves merely because a call was answered. Poland 2050's
two wings suspend their quarrel long enough to accuse us of proving that
cooperation was always camouflage for recruitment.

- @poland_event_queue: Start the telephone calls

@third_way_future_2026
# prose-audit: Grade A — Kosiniak-Kamysz and the new Poland 2050 chair now enact the survival test on the page, its hidden score is replaced by political causes, and both split and survival routes receive bespoke Lewica aftermaths.
title: Third Way faces a second survival test
subtitle: Kosiniak-Kamysz and [+ p2050_leader +] must decide whether a shared threshold still outweighs mutual suspicion
face-image: img/poland/events/pres-candidate-kosiniak.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 27
order: 11
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2026 and month = 1 and third_way_active = 1 and p2050_leader != "Szymon Hołownia"
on-arrival: {!
const thirdWayFutureRoll =
    Math.floor((this.random.uint32() / 4294967296) * 13) - 6;
const thirdWayCombinedVote =
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.psl_vote_intent) || 0) +
    Math.max(0, Number(Q.p2050_vote_intent) || 0);
let futurePressure =
    40 +
    Math.max(0, 58 - (Number(Q.third_way_cohesion) || 0)) * 0.90 -
    Math.max(0, (Number(Q.third_way_cohesion) || 0) - 58) * 0.35 +
    (Number(Q.p2050_coalition_dissent) || 0) * 0.24 +
    (Number(Q.psl_coalition_dissent) || 0) * 0.22 +
    Math.max(
        0,
        45 - (Number(Q.rival_relation_psl_p2050) || 0)
    ) * 0.18 +
    Math.max(0, 10 - (Number(Q.p2050_leadership_margin) || 0)) * 0.45 +
    thirdWayFutureRoll;
if (Q.third_way_response == "Renewed joint list with a written social protocol") {
    futurePressure -= 5;
}
if (Q.third_way_response == "Separate channels under a loose electoral pact") {
    futurePressure += 5;
}
if (thirdWayCombinedVote < 8) {
    futurePressure -= Math.min(6, (8 - thirdWayCombinedVote) * 1.5);
}
if (
    (Number(Q.psl_vote_intent) || 0) >= 5 &&
    (Number(Q.p2050_vote_intent) || 0) >= 5
) {
    futurePressure += 4;
}
Q.third_way_2026_pressure = Math.max(
    0,
    Math.min(100, Math.round(futurePressure))
);
Q.third_way_split = Q.third_way_2026_pressure > 55 ? 1 : 0;
Q.third_way_active = Q.third_way_split ? 0 : 1;
Q.third_way_joint_list = Q.third_way_active ? 1 : 0;
Q.third_way_cohesion += Q.third_way_split ? -20 : 8;
Q.third_way_future = Q.third_way_split
    ? "PSL and Poland 2050 separate after the succession"
    : "Third Way renews its common-list pact through 2027";
Q.news_headline = Q.third_way_split
    ? "Third Way breaks after leadership and coalition pressure overwhelm the pact"
    : "Third Way survives a second internal reckoning";
!}

= January 2026 — Survival is an outcome, not a script

<span class="party-psl"><b>Władysław Kosiniak-Kamysz</b></span>, president of PSL, arrives with a warning from
his county organisations: they will not finance another campaign in which the
partner changes its leadership and its conditions halfway through. **[+
p2050_leader +]**, the new Poland 2050 chair, answers that a joint list cannot
mean permanent submission to PSL's veto.

Hołownia's cross-party talks, the rotation of the Sejm marshal and a close
succession ballot all sit between them. So does the electoral threshold. Their
parties may dislike one another and still fear the ballot separately more.

[? if third_way_split: This time fear is not enough. Kosiniak-Kamysz and [+
p2050_leader +] leave without renewing the agreement. **PSL and Poland 2050
remain separate parties with their existing MPs; only the Third Way pact and
common list end.**?][? if third_way_active: The leaders sign another common-list
agreement. **Third Way survives as two autonomous parties, not as a merger.**
The signatures settle the threshold and leave programme, candidates and money
to the next argument.?]

Lewica now deals either with two newly exposed competitors or with an alliance
whose survival gives it leverage over every unresolved clause. It may offer
equal terms, favour the weaker partner, pay for a real programme or leave the
centre tied together by little more than fear.

- @td2026_bilateral
- @td2026_p2050_shelter
- @td2026_joint_platform
- @td2026_loose_list

@td2026_bilateral
title: Write equal agreements with the two successor parties
subtitle: Recognise the divorce without rewarding either successor for blaming the other.
view-if: third_way_split = 1
on-arrival: third_way_future = "Separate parties under equal parliamentary agreements"; psl_relation += 3; p2050_relation += 3; government_coalition_dissent += 2 if government_party != "pis"; public_trust += 1; news_headline = "The former Third Way parties receive separate written agreements"

Kosiniak-Kamysz and **[+ p2050_leader +]** receive matching invitations and
separate signatures. The agreements cover parliamentary consultation without
recreating Third Way under a different heading. Both parties gain a usable
channel; any cabinet containing their people now has two centrist documents to
reconcile instead of one.

- @poland_event_queue: Sign both agreements

@td2026_p2050_shelter
title: Offer Poland 2050 a list shelter before PSL
subtitle: Rescue the less rooted successor first and let PSL decide whether it prefers pride to access.
view-if: third_way_split = 1
on-arrival: third_way_future = "Poland 2050 offered a separate electoral shelter"; p2050_relation += 6; p2050_coalition_dissent -= 3; psl_relation -= 4; ko_relation -= 2; news_headline = "The new leader receives an electoral offer outside Third Way"

Lewica offers Poland 2050 protected places in a future list negotiation without
claiming its MPs in advance. **[+ p2050_leader +]** accepts the shelter as a
negotiating option, not a merger. Kosiniak-Kamysz sees an attempt to make PSL
the dispensable half of the old pact, while KO sees another bidder entering the
democratic list market.

- @poland_event_queue: Make the offer to Poland 2050

@td2026_joint_platform
title: Finance a joint programme and binding list rules
subtitle: Pay for negotiators who can turn a frightened electoral pact into rules both parties must obey.
view-if: third_way_active = 1
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The joint policy and list secretariat cannot be staffed.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; third_way_future = "Binding Third Way programme and 2027 list rules"; third_way_cohesion += 6; p2050_coalition_dissent -= 3; psl_coalition_dissent -= 3; rival_relation_psl_p2050 += 5; public_trust += 2; news_headline = "Third Way turns survival into a written 2027 pact"

Lewica seconds policy staff to a three-party working table. Kosiniak-Kamysz and
**[+ p2050_leader +]** sign rules for programme disputes, candidate placement
and campaign money before another crisis can improvise them. Third Way remains
their alliance, not ours, but its survival now rests on text rather than the
memory of Hołownia's handshake.

- @poland_event_queue: Second the staff

@td2026_loose_list
title: Keep only the shared threshold and campaign label
subtitle: Preserve the logo and ballot arithmetic, while allowing each party to campaign against the other's programme.
view-if: third_way_active = 1
on-arrival: third_way_future = "Loose Third Way electoral cartel"; p2050_relation += 2; psl_relation += 2; third_way_cohesion -= 2; p2050_coalition_dissent -= 1; psl_coalition_dissent -= 1; public_trust -= 1; news_headline = "Third Way survives as an electoral pact rather than a common programme"

The leaders retain one label and one threshold, then return control of message
and candidates to their own headquarters. The immediate split is avoided.
Voters will still be asked to treat two programmes as one list, and Lewica will
negotiate every serious issue twice.

- @poland_event_queue: Leave the logo where it is

