@reckoning_case_returns_2026
# prose-audit: Grade A — The flagship prosecution's fate is computed from the route the player chose a year earlier rather than announced, the court's reason is procedural and specific, and every response is bounded by what a coalition partner can actually do to a case it does not run.
title: The flagship case comes back from the court
subtitle: Two years of the reckoning meet a judge, and the judge sends the file to the prosecutors who wrote it
face-image: img/poland/events/supreme-court.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 26
order: 12
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2026 and month = 1 and government_party != "pis" and caretaker_government = 0 and reckoning_stage >= 2 and reckoning_case_2026_done = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.reckoning_case_2026_done = 1;
Q.reckoning_stage = 3;
const delivery = Math.max(0, Number(Q.reckoning_delivery) || 0);
// A file built under triage, recovery or an independent prosecution service
// survives partially. A file filed to a deadline does not survive at all.
Q.reckoning_case_outcome = delivery >= 12
    ? "narrowed"
    : delivery >= 4
        ? "returned"
        : "collapsed";
Q.reckoning_convictions =
    Q.reckoning_case_outcome == "narrowed" ? 1 : 0;
Q.reckoning_delivery = Q.reckoning_case_outcome == "collapsed"
    ? Math.max(0, delivery - 6)
    : delivery + 2;
Q.reckoning_pm_pressure =
    (Number(Q.reckoning_pm_pressure) || 12) +
    (Q.reckoning_case_outcome == "collapsed"
        ? 26
        : Q.reckoning_case_outcome == "returned" ? 16 : 6);
Q.public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_salience += 12;
Q.public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_backlash +=
    Q.reckoning_case_outcome == "collapsed" ? 12 : 5;
Q.institutional_trust = Math.max(
    0,
    (Number(Q.institutional_trust) || 0) -
        (Q.reckoning_case_outcome == "collapsed" ? 5 : 2)
);
Q.pis_poll_momentum =
    (Number(Q.pis_poll_momentum) || 0) +
    (Q.reckoning_case_outcome == "collapsed" ? 0.35 : 0.1);
Q.news_headline = Q.reckoning_case_outcome == "collapsed"
    ? "The reckoning's flagship indictment is sent back in its entirety"
    : Q.reckoning_case_outcome == "returned"
        ? "The court returns most of the reckoning's flagship indictment"
        : "One count of the flagship indictment survives to trial";
!}

= January 2026 — What a courtroom does to a press conference

The first indictment the reckoning treated as its own reaches a Warsaw
courtroom, and the presiding judge does what judges do with an indictment
assembled at speed: reads it against the file behind it.

[? if reckoning_case_outcome = "collapsed": The whole thing goes back.
Counts drafted from press reporting rather than from evidence, witnesses
listed who were never questioned, an expert opinion commissioned after the
charges were framed. The court does not rule that the defendants are innocent.
It rules that this document cannot be tried, which on television is the same
sentence.?]
[? if reckoning_case_outcome = "returned": Most of it goes back for
supplementation, and the reasons are procedural rather than exculpatory: gaps
in the chain of documents, counts framed more broadly than the evidence
supports. What remains is real and has lost two years.?]
[? if reckoning_case_outcome = "narrowed": One count survives, narrowed to what
the paperwork can carry, and it is going to trial. It is a fraction of what was
announced in 2024 and it is the first thing in this entire chapter that a court
has agreed to hear.?]

The defence adds the argument everybody knew was coming: that the judge's own
appointment is one this government calls defective, so whatever happens next
can be attacked from either direction by whoever loses.

By the evening **[+ prime_minister +]** has said in public that the pace of the
reckoning is unacceptable, which is the first time the Prime Minister has
attacked the delivery of a ministry [? if left_in_government = 1: inside this
cabinet?][? if left_in_government = 0: in this cabinet?] rather than the
courts, the President or PiS.
[? if reckoning_team_active = 1: **Roman Giertych** says the ministry has been
timid; the Justice Ministry says the ministry has been lawful. Both statements
are briefed to the same journalists within an hour.?]
[? if reckoning_team_active = 0: The Chancellery's briefers say the ministry has
been timid; the Justice Ministry says it has been lawful. Both statements reach
the same journalists within an hour.?]

- @reckoning_case_rebuild
- @reckoning_case_institutions
- @reckoning_case_expectation
- @reckoning_case_blame

@reckoning_case_rebuild
title: Fund the rebuild: prosecutors, analysts and one competent case
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Money and staff for the files that survive, instead of another announcement about the ones that did not.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: There is no capacity to fight a staffing budget through the coalition this month.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; reckoning_case_response = "Rebuild"; reckoning_delivery += 10; reckoning_noise -= 4; reckoning_pm_pressure -= 8; prosecution_oversight_capacity += 5; judicial_legitimacy += 3; institutional_trust += 3; government_delivery += 2; ko_relation += 2; public_trust += 2; news_headline = "The coalition funds prosecutors and analysts instead of announcing new charges"

We put the argument in numbers: the economic-crime units that have to try these
cases are staffed at roughly the level they had when they were only expected to
handle ordinary fraud. Financial analysts, translators, digital forensics, and
protection for the prosecutors whose careers were built by the people they are
now investigating.

It is a budget line, it is invisible, and it is the difference between the next
indictment being tried and being returned. Nobody will remember that we asked
for it, including us, until something is finally convicted.

- @poland_event_queue: Fund the rebuild

@reckoning_case_institutions
title: Say the true thing: the courts have to be repaired before they can convict
subtitle: Put the defective appointments, not the ministry, at the centre — and accept being accused of defending the accused.
on-arrival: reckoning_case_response = "Institutions first"; reckoning_delivery += 4; reckoning_noise -= 6; judicial_repair_mandate += 6; constitutional_restraint += 4; judicial_legitimacy += 4; institutional_trust += 3; public_trust -= 1; left_poll_momentum -= 0.2; giertych_standing -= 4; news_headline = "Lewica says no reckoning can be finished in courts this government calls defective"

We say it in the chamber, with the defence's own submission quoted back: a
government that describes a court as unlawfully composed cannot then be
surprised when convictions obtained there are attacked on that ground. The
courts have to be repaired first, and repairing them is slower than any
election cycle.

It is correct, it is unanswerable, and it sounds exactly like an excuse.
Republika runs it under a caption about the Left defending Ziobro's people, and
enough of our own voters believe the caption to make the week expensive.

- @poland_event_queue: Make the institutional argument

@reckoning_case_expectation
title: Tell the public what a reckoning can actually deliver, and by when
subtitle: Kill the promise before it kills the government; the honesty is a one-week political injury and a two-year insurance policy.
on-arrival: reckoning_case_response = "Reset expectations"; reckoning_noise -= 10; reckoning_pm_pressure -= 12; public_trust += 4; institutional_trust += 2; left_poll_momentum -= 0.3; ko_relation -= 3; giertych_standing -= 7; progressive_credibility += 3; news_headline = "The Left tells voters what a reckoning can and cannot produce before 2027"

Our spokespeople stop promising verdicts. They give a calendar: which cases can
realistically reach trial before the election, which cannot, what a recovered
złoty looks like against a conviction, and how long an appeal takes in Poland.

We lose a third of a point immediately, because a party that explains is a
party that is failing. What we buy is that nobody can produce a clip of us
promising a jailed minister in 2027, and that when the Prime Minister goes
looking for somebody to blame for the pace, our ministers are the ones who
already published the truth about it.

- @poland_event_queue: Publish the calendar

@reckoning_case_blame
title: Blame the ministry and demand a faster hand on it
subtitle: Join the Prime Minister's attack on his own justice minister; the reckoning gets a scapegoat and somebody in KO gets a vacancy to want.
on-arrival: reckoning_case_response = "Blame the ministry"; reckoning_noise += 10; reckoning_pm_pressure += 14; giertych_standing += 12; ko_right_score += 3; reckoning_delivery -= 4; judicial_legitimacy -= 3; institutional_trust -= 3; left_poll_momentum += 0.2; ko_relation += 3; government_procedural_restraint -= 4; news_headline = "The coalition partners join the attack on their own justice ministry"

We add our voice to the Chancellery's: the ministry has been slow, cautious and
too respectful of institutions that were captured to be disrespected. It is a
free week of agreeing with the public.

[? if reckoning_team_active = 1: Every sentence of it is an argument for
replacing the minister, and there is exactly one person in this coalition who
has spent two years building the case that he would be faster. We have not
chosen him. We have written his job application.?]
[? if reckoning_team_active = 0: Every sentence of it is an argument for
replacing the minister, and we have no idea who the Chancellery has in mind. We
have not chosen the successor. We have written the vacancy notice.?]

- @poland_event_queue: Join the attack
